<title>UK: UK notes in circulation rise 4.1 pct in week.</title>
<headline>UK notes in circulation rise 4.1 pct in week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>British bank notes in circulation rose 4.1 percent in the week to Dec 31 over the equivalent year-ago week, data released by the Bank of England showed. Last week the rise was 6.8 percent.</p>
<p>NOTES IN CIRCULATION (in rounded bln stg) -</p>
<p>				Latest week  pvs week	yr-ago week</p>
<p> Notes in circulation     22.6	   23.19	   21.72</p>
<p> Bankers' deposits	  2.44	   2.07	     2.13</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7715</p>
</text>
